{"author":{"id":"aefab16712695e4f092f7bad7c1285ac48ce0d1ef6cc283cea20b3795ed9457a"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788771167,"nonce":"QHHsKcTfHufPrj/QY9RL+SCXlNw=","message":"Root cause:\nConcurrent collab serve daemons prior to file locks or non-atomic batch writes appended multiple JSON objects onto a single physical line without an intervening newline. In src/server/mod.rs, replay() used serde_json::from_str::\u003cEvent\u003e(line), failing with 'trailing characters at line 1 column 263' on concatenated lines. In /Volumes/extension/code/zterm, line 11946 of journal.jsonl had two concatenated KeepaliveUpdated events, blocking replay and daemon startup.\n\nFix (commit 15479c3b in collab):\n1. In src/server/mod.rs, replaced serde_json::from_str with streaming deserializer serde_json::Deserializer::from_str(trimmed).into_iter::\u003cEvent\u003e(). If a physical line contains multiple concatenated valid events, all are applied in order and convert_root is flagged so journal.jsonl is automatically self-healed and rewritten into clean 1-event-per-line format on startup.\n2. Pre-buffer batch commits into a single byte buffer with trailing newline before write_all and sync_data.\n3. Added peer test concatenated_journal_events_replay_and_self_heal. All 108 tests pass.\n4. Compiled and deployed to /Users/fanzhang/.cargo/bin/collab.\n\nVerification:\nDaemon in /Volumes/extension/code/zterm successfully restarted and self-healed line 11946 into two clean lines without data loss. collab who and collab status now return cleanly.","files":null}]}